    "description": "Heap OOB read in OT::kern::has_data() when it reads a 32-bit big-endian field from a truncated 'kern' table without sufficient length validation. The PoC provides a tiny font blob where the kern table header advertises data but the actual table ends exactly before the 4-byte read, so BEInt<unsigned int,4>::operator unsigned int() dereferences past the blob end. Crash manifests in hb-machinery.hh during BEInt conversion, but root cause is missing bounds check in kern-table parsing logic.",
    "conditions": "Triggered via hb-shape-fuzzer with a minimal crafted font input (including a 'kern' table) that passes initial table discovery/sanitization enough to reach hb_ot_layout_has_kerning() -> OT::kern::has_data(). Input must make has_data() inspect a 4-byte field at/near end-of-table while actual blob length is shorter than required, causing a 1-byte read past allocation boundary during shape-plan compilation."
